 35CL    32S(A,PG)                     1970HO09,1972BR33,1973AL22ENSDF    202509
 35CL  H TYP=FUL$AUT=LIJIE SUN AND JUN CHEN$                                    
 35CL2 H CIT=ENSDF$CUT=30-Sep-2025$                                             
 35CL  H TYP=FUL$AUT=JUN CHEN, JOHN CAMERON AND BALRAJ SINGH$                   
 35CL2 H CIT=NDS 112,2715 (2011)$CUT=20-Oct-2011$                               
 35CL dL E$Least-squares fitting is done by GLSC (version 19-Aug-2025)          
 35CL c  J|p=0+ for {+32}S ground state.                                        
 35CL c  1970Ho09: 10.975-, 11.960-, 12.120-MeV |a beams were produced from the 
 35CL2c  Chalk River MP tandem accelerator. Targets were 100-|mg/cm{+2}         
 35CL3c  Sb{-2}S{-3} on a 10-|mg/cm{+2} carbon backing. |g rays were detected   
 35CL4c  using 15.2-cm-long by 12.7-cm-diam NaI(Tl) detectors. Protons were     
 35CL5c  detected using an annular silicon surface detector close to 180|' with 
 35CL6c  FWHM=30 keV for protons and FWHM=50 keV for |a. Measured E{-p}, E|g,   
 35CL7c  I|g, p|g(|q). Deduced 25 level energies from E{-p}, J, branching       
 35CL8c  ratios, multipole mixing ratios.                                       
 35CL d                                                                         
 35CL c  1972Br33: a 10-MeV |a beam was produced from the Chalk River MP tandem 
 35CL2c  accelerator. Targets were 340-|mg/cm{+2} Sb{-2}S{-3} on gold backings. 
 35CL3c  |g rays were detected using a 44-cm{+3} Ge(Li) detector inside an      
 35CL4c  anticoincidence split annular NaI(Tl) detector. Measured E|g, I|g.     
 35CL5c  Deduced 11 level energies, 16 |g branching ratios, 11 lifetimes using  
 35CL6c  the Doppler Shift Attenuation Method (DSAM). 1970In01 from the same    
 35CL7c  experiment deduced the lifetime using DSAM for a level at 3942 keV and 
 35CL8c  the mixing ratio for a 3942->2646 |g transition.                       
 35CL d                                                                         
 35CL c  1973Al22: a 14-MeV |a beam was produced from the 80-cm cyclotron at    
 35CL2c  cyclotron at the Research Institute for Physics in Stockholm and       
 35CL3c  12-16-MeV |a beams were produced from the Uppsala tandem accelerator.  
 35CL4c  Targets were prepared by depositing pulverized sulphur enriched to     
 35CL5c  99.9% in {+32}S on lead backings. |g rays were detected using an Ortec 
 35CL6c  60-cm{+3} Ge(Li) detector with FWHM=2.2 keV at 1333 keV and an         
 35CL7c  additional Canberra 60-cm{+3} Ge(Li) detector for |g|g-coincidence     
 35CL8c  measurements. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g-coin, 4 |g(|q). Deduced 12 level 
 35CL9c  energies from E|g, J for 4 levels, branching ratios, and mixing ratios.
 35CL d                                                                         
 35CL c  1969In04: 6-8-MeV |a beams were produced from the Chalk River MP tandem
 35CL2c  accelerator. A thick target (270 |mg/cm{+2}) of natural sulfur on a    
 35CL3c  tantalum backing and a thin target (50 |mg/cm{+2}) of Sb{-2}S{-3} on a 
 35CL4c  gold backing were used. |g rays were detected using two Ge(Li)         
 35CL5c  detectors of 15 and 40 cm{+3} volume. Measured E|g, I|g. Deduced 6     
 35CL6c  level energies, branching ratios, 5 lifetimes using the Doppler Shift  
 35CL7c  Attenuation Method (DSAM) and 1 lifetime for the 3163-keV level using  
 35CL8c  the Recoil Distance Method (RDM), and transition strengths.            
 35CL d                                                                         
 35CL c  1974Lo17: 11.0, 12.0 and 14.7-MeV |a beams were produced from the      
 35CL2c  Oliver Lodge Laboratory at the University of Liverpool. Targets were   
 35CL3c  natural sulphur in CdS. Protons were detected using an annular |DE-E   
 35CL4c  telescope close to 180|' with FWHM=80 keV. |g rays were detected using 
 35CL5c  five NaI(Tl) and one Ge(Li) detectors. Measured E|g, I|g, p|g-coin,    
 35CL6c  |g|g-coin, |g-ray linear polarization. Deduced J and |p for 3 levels, 6
 35CL7c  |g branching ratios, 5 mixing ratios, and lifetimes for a 5408-keV     
 35CL8c  level using DSAM and for a 6088-keV level using RDM.                   
 35CL d                                                                         
 35CL c  1973Br26: a 11.2-MeV |a beam was produced from the Legnaro (Padova) Van
 35CL2c  de Graaff generator. Targets were natural CdS. |g rays were detected   
 35CL3c  using a Ge(Li) detector. Deduced the lifetime using the Recoil Distance
 35CL4c  Method (RDM) for a level at 3163 keV.                                  
 35CL d                                                                         
 35CL c  1973An01: 5.5- and 8.6-MeV |a beams of 100-200 nA were produced from   
 35CL2c  the Oxford Vertical Van de Graaff (Injector) or the Oxford E(n) Tandem.
 35CL3c  Targets were natural sulphur in AgS. |g rays were detected using a     
 35CL4c  Ge(Li) detector at 0|'. Deduced the lifetime using the Recoil Distance 
 35CL5c  Method (RDM) for a level at 3163 keV.                                  
 35CL d                                                                         
 35CL cG E$1973Al22 is the only literature in this dataset that reported        
 35CL2cG measured E|g with uncertainties. 1969In04 and 1972Br33 reported        
 35CL3cG E(level) with uncertainties derived from their measured E|g but did not
 35CL4cG report E|g. Evaluators adopt the uncertainties of E(level) from        
 35CL5cG 1969In04 and 1972Br33 as the uncertainties of an E|g if this |g        
 35CL6cG transition populates the ground state and is also the dominant decay   
 35CL7cG branch of that level. Other E|g values without uncertainties are from  
 35CL8cG level-energy differences.                                              
 35CL cL E$From a least-squares fit to E|g values with uncertainties, unless    
 35CL2cL otherwise noted. 1970Ho09 reported E(level) with uncertainties derived 
 35CL3cL from measured E{-p}.                                                   
